# 6. Improvement and Defect Management

The next phase is incremental improvement, not completion of a list of old implementation tasks.

Classify future work as follows:

| Classification | Meaning |
|---|---|
| Completed baseline | Already delivered and working in the current application |
| Improvement | A refinement to an existing working experience |
| Future capability | A deliberately deferred product capability outside the current scope |
| Defect | A confirmed regression or failure in existing behavior |

Rules:
1. Capture newly identified improvements in Platform Backlog.
2. Do not automatically begin every item in the backlog.
3. Mario selects the next improvement before implementation.
4. Preserve existing behavior and saved data unless the requested change explicitly requires otherwise.
5. Treat a confirmed regression as a defect, not as evidence that the entire application is unfinished.
6. Do not reopen completed work because an older Waypoint or historical backlog section has stale status wording.

